1
00:00:00,241 --> 00:00:02,150
Last video ended on a chessboard.

2
00:00:02,731 --> 00:00:04,253
One grain of rice on the first square,

3
00:00:04,694 --> 00:00:07,357
two on the second, then four, eight and

4
00:00:07,418 --> 00:00:12,084
sixteen, with running totals one, three, seven, fifteen

5
00:00:12,385 --> 00:00:13,065
and thirty-one.

6
00:00:13,851 --> 00:00:14,500
Look at the totals.

7
00:00:15,008 --> 00:00:17,123
Each one is one less than a power

8
00:00:17,164 --> 00:00:17,466
of two.

9
00:00:18,173 --> 00:00:20,268
Thirty-one is thirty-two minus one.

10
00:00:21,112 --> 00:00:23,313
If the pattern keeps going, the first ten

11
00:00:23,394 --> 00:00:26,054
squares hold two to the ten, minus one

12
00:00:26,135 --> 00:00:28,416
grains, which is one thousand and twenty-three.

13
00:00:29,257 --> 00:00:30,792
But a pattern isn't a reason.

14
00:00:31,419 --> 00:00:32,222
Why does it work,

15
00:00:32,725 --> 00:00:34,594
and does something like it work for every

16
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:35,498
geometric sequence?

17
00:00:36,168 --> 00:00:37,635
Here's the reason, with a small case.

18
00:00:38,419 --> 00:00:41,212
Take two minus one, times one plus two

19
00:00:41,293 --> 00:00:42,156
plus four plus eight.

20
00:00:42,921 --> 00:00:44,835
Two minus one is just one, so this

21
00:00:44,896 --> 00:00:45,560
is the sum itself.

22
00:00:46,308 --> 00:00:47,357
Now expand the brackets.

23
00:00:48,124 --> 00:00:50,571
Two times the bracket gives two, four, eight

24
00:00:50,712 --> 00:00:51,333
and sixteen.

25
00:00:52,057 --> 00:00:54,160
On the board, doubling every pile gives the

26
00:00:54,222 --> 00:00:56,526
next square's pile, so the whole row slides

27
00:00:56,707 --> 00:00:57,388
one square along.

28
00:00:58,271 --> 00:01:00,495
Minus one times the bracket gives minus one,

29
00:01:00,816 --> 00:01:02,840
minus two, minus four and minus eight.

30
00:01:03,603 --> 00:01:05,529
Line them up, and the middle terms cancel

31
00:01:05,570 --> 00:01:06,031
in pairs.

32
00:01:06,855 --> 00:01:07,978
Only two terms survive:

33
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:09,945
sixteen, and minus one.

34
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:11,922
So the sum is sixteen minus one.

35
00:01:12,795 --> 00:01:15,522
Take x minus one, times x to the

36
00:01:15,703 --> 00:01:17,888
n minus one, plus x to the n

37
00:01:17,929 --> 00:01:18,590
minus two,

38
00:01:19,092 --> 00:01:21,157
and so on, down to x, plus one.

39
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:24,665
Multiplying the bracket by x raises every power

40
00:01:24,706 --> 00:01:27,070
by one, so the top term becomes x

41
00:01:27,111 --> 00:01:27,531
to the n.

42
00:01:28,314 --> 00:01:30,739
Multiplying by minus one gives the same powers

43
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:32,163
as before, all negative.

44
00:01:32,906 --> 00:01:35,009
Every power from x up to x to

45
00:01:35,050 --> 00:01:37,092
the n minus one appears once with a

46
00:01:37,133 --> 00:01:39,436
plus and once with a minus, so they

47
00:01:39,478 --> 00:01:39,817
cancel.

48
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,607
What's left is x to the n, minus

49
00:01:42,729 --> 00:01:42,848
one.

50
00:01:43,692 --> 00:01:45,939
Nothing here depended on which whole number n

51
00:01:46,121 --> 00:01:48,528
is, so it's true for every whole number

52
00:01:48,710 --> 00:01:49,612
from one upward.

53
00:01:50,342 --> 00:01:52,639
Now use it to add any geometric sequence.

54
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:55,510
S sub n is a, plus a r,

55
00:01:55,691 --> 00:01:58,018
plus a r squared, up to a r

56
00:01:58,060 --> 00:01:59,062
to the n minus one.

57
00:01:59,705 --> 00:02:01,592
Take out the a, and the bracket is

58
00:02:01,653 --> 00:02:04,142
exactly the one we just expanded, with r

59
00:02:04,244 --> 00:02:04,986
in place of x.

60
00:02:05,589 --> 00:02:07,938
So r minus one, times S sub n,

61
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,568
is a, times r to the n, minus

62
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:10,809
one.

63
00:02:11,494 --> 00:02:13,540
To get S sub n alone, divide by

64
00:02:13,561 --> 00:02:14,363
r minus one.

65
00:02:15,047 --> 00:02:17,438
That's only allowed if r isn't one, because

66
00:02:17,459 --> 00:02:18,825
then we'd be dividing by zero.

67
00:02:19,388 --> 00:02:21,452
And if r is one, every term is

68
00:02:21,473 --> 00:02:23,818
a, so the sum is just n lots

69
00:02:23,859 --> 00:02:24,159
of a.

70
00:02:24,814 --> 00:02:27,137
Multiply the top and bottom by minus one,

71
00:02:27,499 --> 00:02:28,940
and you get the form in the syllabus:

72
00:02:29,782 --> 00:02:32,245
a, times one minus r to the n,

73
00:02:32,707 --> 00:02:33,547
all over one minus r.

74
00:02:35,413 --> 00:02:37,439
Both forms always give the same value.

75
00:02:38,002 --> 00:02:40,087
When r is bigger than one, the r

76
00:02:40,108 --> 00:02:42,112
minus one form keeps the top and bottom

77
00:02:42,153 --> 00:02:42,553
positive.

78
00:02:43,296 --> 00:02:45,505
When r is between minus one and one,

79
00:02:45,907 --> 00:02:47,835
the one minus r form does.

80
00:02:48,821 --> 00:02:51,132
Some books get S sub n by multiplying

81
00:02:51,174 --> 00:02:52,540
it by r and subtracting.

82
00:02:53,144 --> 00:02:55,130
That's the same shift and cancel, done row

83
00:02:55,151 --> 00:02:55,512
by row.

84
00:02:56,222 --> 00:02:58,215
So how much rice is on the whole

85
00:02:58,296 --> 00:02:58,799
chessboard?

86
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:01,124
Here a is one, r

87
00:03:02,004 --> 00:03:04,707
is two and n is sixty-four, so the

88
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:08,010
total is two to the sixty-four, minus one.

89
00:03:08,691 --> 00:03:12,039
That's about eighteen billion billion grains, which is

90
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:14,305
hundreds of years of the whole world's rice

91
00:03:14,345 --> 00:03:14,726
harvest.

92
00:03:15,388 --> 00:03:17,895
The last square alone holds more than all

93
00:03:17,935 --> 00:03:19,239
the other squares put together.

94
00:03:19,981 --> 00:03:20,469
Let's use it.

95
00:03:20,955 --> 00:03:23,338
Find the sum from k equals one to

96
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,344
six of three times two to the k

97
00:03:26,365 --> 00:03:26,945
minus one.

98
00:03:27,828 --> 00:03:31,215
The rule gives three, six, twelve, so a

99
00:03:31,276 --> 00:03:33,360
is three and r is two.

100
00:03:34,164 --> 00:03:36,474
The counter goes from one to six, so

101
00:03:36,535 --> 00:03:37,499
there are six terms.

102
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,616
Since r is bigger than one, use the

103
00:03:40,939 --> 00:03:41,964
r minus one form.

104
00:03:42,528 --> 00:03:45,398
That's three, times two to the six, minus

105
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:45,740
one,

106
00:03:46,303 --> 00:03:47,588
over two minus one.

107
00:03:48,371 --> 00:03:50,458
Two to the six is sixty-four, so it's

108
00:03:50,599 --> 00:03:53,107
three times sixty-three, which is one hundred and

109
00:03:53,208 --> 00:03:53,729
eighty-nine.

110
00:03:54,594 --> 00:03:56,646
Adding the six terms one by one gives

111
00:03:56,708 --> 00:03:57,452
the same total.

112
00:03:58,162 --> 00:03:59,707
Signs need care when r

113
00:04:00,229 --> 00:04:00,731
is negative.

114
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:03,559
Find the sum of the first six terms

115
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:07,872
of one, minus three, plus nine, minus twenty-seven,

116
00:04:08,113 --> 00:04:08,634
and so on.

117
00:04:09,316 --> 00:04:11,834
Here a is one, and r is minus

118
00:04:11,894 --> 00:04:12,156
three.

119
00:04:12,979 --> 00:04:15,827
Use the one minus r form, with brackets

120
00:04:15,947 --> 00:04:16,990
around minus three.

121
00:04:17,772 --> 00:04:19,816
Minus three to the six is seven hundred

122
00:04:19,837 --> 00:04:21,980
and twenty-nine, because an even power of a

123
00:04:22,042 --> 00:04:23,103
negative is positive.

124
00:04:23,804 --> 00:04:26,289
So the top is one minus seven hundred

125
00:04:26,309 --> 00:04:28,854
and twenty-nine, and the bottom is one plus

126
00:04:29,074 --> 00:04:30,196
three, which is four.

127
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:33,066
The sum is minus seven hundred and twenty-eight

128
00:04:33,187 --> 00:04:35,576
over four, which is minus one hundred and

129
00:04:35,657 --> 00:04:36,118
eighty-two.

130
00:04:36,695 --> 00:04:38,722
One more, with a ratio less than one.

131
00:04:39,927 --> 00:04:41,793
Find the sum of the first eight terms

132
00:04:42,135 --> 00:04:45,224
of sixty-four, plus thirty-two, plus sixteen,

133
00:04:45,747 --> 00:04:46,127
and so on.

134
00:04:46,991 --> 00:04:47,250
Here a

135
00:04:47,933 --> 00:04:49,978
is sixty-four and r is a half.

136
00:04:50,921 --> 00:04:52,743
Use the one minus r form:

137
00:04:53,386 --> 00:04:55,909
sixty-four, times one minus a half to the

138
00:04:55,970 --> 00:04:56,149
eight,

139
00:04:56,711 --> 00:04:57,772
over one minus a half.

140
00:04:58,895 --> 00:05:01,299
Dividing by a half doubles, so that's one

141
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:04,265
hundred and twenty-eight, times one minus one over

142
00:05:04,326 --> 00:05:05,307
two hundred and fifty-six.

143
00:05:06,069 --> 00:05:08,036
That's one hundred and twenty-eight, minus a half,

144
00:05:08,559 --> 00:05:10,466
so the sum is one hundred and twenty-seven

145
00:05:10,568 --> 00:05:11,008
and a half.

146
00:05:11,793 --> 00:05:13,466
Notice how close that is to one hundred

147
00:05:13,487 --> 00:05:14,010
and twenty-eight.

148
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:15,843
Here's the idea to remember.

149
00:05:16,589 --> 00:05:20,193
Multiplying by r shifts every term one step

150
00:05:20,234 --> 00:05:20,514
along.

151
00:05:21,197 --> 00:05:23,924
Subtract, and only the new end and the

152
00:05:24,065 --> 00:05:25,168
old start are left.

153
00:05:25,891 --> 00:05:27,997
That's why the formula has r to the

154
00:05:28,199 --> 00:05:30,125
n, minus one, inside it.

155
00:05:32,786 --> 00:05:33,216
Your turn.

156
00:05:33,843 --> 00:05:36,368
Evaluate the sum from k equals one to

157
00:05:36,449 --> 00:05:38,934
five of two times three to the k

158
00:05:38,954 --> 00:05:39,516
minus one.

159
00:05:40,082 --> 00:05:40,874
Pause here to answer.

160
00:05:51,568 --> 00:05:54,498
The terms are two, six, eighteen, and so

161
00:05:54,579 --> 00:05:56,967
on, so a is two and r is

162
00:05:57,109 --> 00:05:57,389
three.

163
00:05:58,093 --> 00:06:00,204
The counter runs from one to five, so

164
00:06:00,245 --> 00:06:01,230
there are five terms.

165
00:06:01,995 --> 00:06:04,640
The sum is two, times three to the

166
00:06:04,721 --> 00:06:07,726
five, minus one, over three minus one, which

167
00:06:07,787 --> 00:06:09,029
is two hundred and forty-two.

168
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:10,789
Eighty is wrong.

169
00:06:11,194 --> 00:06:13,238
It uses three to the four, the last

170
00:06:13,259 --> 00:06:15,685
term's power, instead of n, which is five.

171
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:17,824
Last one.

172
00:06:18,635 --> 00:06:21,119
In a geometric sequence, the second term is

173
00:06:21,261 --> 00:06:23,685
six and the fifth term is forty-eight.

174
00:06:24,629 --> 00:06:26,677
Find the sum of the first eight terms.

175
00:06:27,523 --> 00:06:28,170
Pause here to answer.

176
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:41,182
From the second term to the fifth is

177
00:06:41,342 --> 00:06:45,405
three multiplications, so r cubed is forty-eight over

178
00:06:45,525 --> 00:06:48,287
six, which is eight, and r is two.

179
00:06:48,987 --> 00:06:51,622
Then a times two is six, so a

180
00:06:51,763 --> 00:06:52,266
is three.

181
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:55,416
The sum of eight terms is three, times

182
00:06:55,556 --> 00:06:57,541
two to the eight, minus one, which is

183
00:06:57,621 --> 00:06:58,824
seven hundred and sixty-five.

184
00:06:59,809 --> 00:07:02,166
One thousand five hundred and thirty is wrong.

185
00:07:02,407 --> 00:07:04,494
It starts the sum at six, the second

186
00:07:04,515 --> 00:07:05,538
term, instead of a.

187
00:07:07,461 --> 00:07:10,252
So the shift-and-cancel expansion gives the sum of

188
00:07:10,433 --> 00:07:12,702
any n terms, as long as r isn't

189
00:07:12,883 --> 00:07:12,983
one.

190
00:07:13,946 --> 00:07:15,469
Drop a tennis ball from one hundred and

191
00:07:15,509 --> 00:07:18,575
twenty-eight centimetres, and suppose each bounce reaches half

192
00:07:18,615 --> 00:07:19,677
the height it fell from.

193
00:07:20,479 --> 00:07:24,566
Its bounce heights are sixty-four, thirty-two, sixteen, and

194
00:07:24,606 --> 00:07:24,927
so on,

195
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:27,631
and each new height fills half of the

196
00:07:27,712 --> 00:07:30,076
gap that's left below one hundred and twenty-eight.

197
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,458
What happens if the ball never stops bouncing?

198
00:07:35,988 --> 00:07:36,871
Here are the key notes.

199
00:07:37,394 --> 00:07:39,162
Pause the video if you need more time

200
00:07:39,183 --> 00:07:39,664
to copy them.
